Closes #948

## Root cause
`session_shutdown` (`packages/pi-fff/src/index.ts:866`) ignored the ctx pi passes and `destroyFinder()` -> `stopHomeScanStatus()` (`:530`) went through `uiCtx`, which was captured on `session_start`. If one extension instance outlives a session replacement, that ctx is stale and its `ui` getter throws. `stopHomeScanStatus()` ran first in `destroyFinder()`, so the throw also skipped `mainFinder.destroy()` / `auxPool.destroy()` and leaked the finders.

## Fix
`session_shutdown` sets `uiCtx` to the event's ctx before teardown and clears it after. `destroyFinder()` frees the finder and pool first and clears the UI status last, so a UI throw cannot leak native resources. Plain `pi` CLI is unaffected either way: it builds new services per replacement, so each session gets a fresh closure.

## Steps to reproduce
Needs global pi (`npm i -g @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent`, checked on 0.86.1, which already has the stale guard) and bun. The native finder is mocked; everything else is the real SDK.
```sh
mkdir -p /tmp/r948 && cd /tmp/r948   # save the file below as repro.test.ts
HOME=/tmp/r948 REPO=/path/to/fff bun test ./repro.test.ts
```
```ts
import { expect, mock, test } from "bun:test";
const PI = "/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent"; // global pi install
const destroy = mock(() => {});
const finder = { isDestroyed: false, destroy, waitForScan: async () => {}, getScanProgress: () => ({ ok: false }) };
const fff = { FileFinder: { create: () => ({ ok: true, value: finder }) } };
mock.module("@ff-labs/fff-node", () => fff);
mock.module("@ff-labs/fff-bun", () => fff);
const tui = await import(`${PI}/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-tui/dist/index.js`);
mock.module("@earendil-works/pi-tui", () => tui);
const tb = await import(`${PI}/node_modules/typebox/build/index.mjs`);
mock.module("@sinclair/typebox", () => tb);
const sdk = await import(`${PI}/dist/index.js`);
const { default: ext } = await import(`${process.env.REPO}/packages/pi-fff/src/index.ts`);

test("#948", async () => {
  const cwd = process.cwd();
  const services = await sdk.createAgentSessionServices({ cwd, agentDir: `${cwd}/agent`,
    resourceLoaderOptions: { noExtensions: true, noSkills: true, noContextFiles: true, extensionFactories: [ext] } });
  const open = () => sdk.createAgentSessionFromServices({ services, sessionManager: sdk.SessionManager.inMemory(cwd) });
  const a = await open();
  await a.session.bindExtensions({ uiContext: new Proxy({}, { get: () => () => {} }) });
  const b = await open(); // replacement session, same extension instance, never bound
  a.session.dispose();
  const errors: string[] = [];
  b.session.extensionRunner.onError((e: any) => errors.push(`${e.event}: ${e.error}`));
  await b.session.extensionRunner.emit({ type: "session_shutdown", reason: "quit" });
  console.log({ errors, finderDestroyed: destroy.mock.calls.length > 0 });
  expect(errors).toEqual([]);
});
```
Expected: `errors: []`, `finderDestroyed: true`. Actual on `main`:
```
errors: [ "session_shutdown: This extension ctx is stale after session replacement or reload. Do not use a captured pi or command ctx after ctx.newSession(), ..." ],
finderDestroyed: false,
```

## How verified
- Repro above: fails on `origin/main` (worktree), passes on this branch (`errors: []`, `finderDestroyed: true`).
- New test `session_shutdown uses its own ctx and still destroys the finder` in `packages/pi-fff/test/extension.test.ts`: fails with `src/index.ts` from main, passes with the fix.
- `cd packages/pi-fff && bun test test/`: 110 pass, 0 fail.
- `bunx oxfmt@0.63.0 --check` and `bunx oxlint@1.78.0` on the changed files: clean.

